{"id":"tearing_cloth","compound_name":"Graphs::MPM::tearing_cloth","source_path":"tearing_cloth/tearing_cloth.json","category":"Cloth","author":"Autodesk","description":"An MPM simulation of cloth tearing through constraints","documentation_file":"tearing_cloth_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"# Tearing Cloth\n\n### What it does\n\nThis graph demonstrates the tearing of cloth through constraints.\n\n### Inputs and Outputs\n\nA basic Bifrost plane is the input cloth geometry. Two cubes, one which is animated for scale are inputs to the constrain_mpm compound. The output is the simulated cloth mesh. It's normals are updated and a referenced material is applied for display.\n\n### Useful information\n\n- The animated cube constraint is used to demonstrate bunching of the cloth when it shrinks, and tearing of the cloth when it expands. \n\n- The stretchiness and bounciness of the cloth is set by the `viscosity` and `vibration speed` properties.\n\n- The tearing behavior is controlled in the Failure section of the make_mpm_cloth compound.  By settings `failure_post_process` to something other than no failure, the cloth with tear.  What happens after it tears is determined by the post process selected. In this case, subdivide and split will ensure that the appropriate amount of triangles are added to the mesh at tearing time to achieve the level of detail required by the solve.  \n\n- The `tearing_threshold` property is set with a fractal_noise_field, which adds weak spots to the cloth and creates anisotropic tearing patterns.","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9","fields":"2.15.0.9","geometries":"2.15.0.9","mpm":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[{"portName":"static_cube_constraint","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"animated_cube_constraint","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"cloth","portDirection":"output","portType":"array<Object>"}],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"false"}